lass=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1467728-v5-timeline?p=1467751#post1467751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you might have some dates wrong. I'm not sure where you got 2016 from.<br /> <br /> Per page 544, the events of Beckett's Jyhad Diary take place, and conclude, in 2005.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was my original understanding, but following a discussion in another topic (the Death of Melinda Galbraith) we concluded that the Palla Grande must be taking place in at least 2016. Chiefly because Vasantasena references the fact that the regent has been dead for 16 years.<br /> <br /> According to both Mexico City by Night and Revised: Clanbook Tzimisce, Galbraith dies 2000/2001 and is then impersonated by Sikorsky. Assuming the Galbraith that dies at the Palla Grande Beckett and Lucita attend is Sikorsky (in the guise of Galbraith), then this would imply it takes place either 2016/2017. The only alternative is it happened at a Palla Grande between '02 and '05, but then there's no evidence (that I saw at least) as to which year it would be.<br /> <br /> Originally I thought it all might've happened in 2000, with Galbraith dying, then being impersonated, only for Sikorsky to die shortly after. But BJD also alludes to a conspiracy to cover up Sikorsky's impersonation having been going for a while, which seems to preclude that theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link